# agi engine. Never committed here; the engine is a separate repo that agi-tree
# is the development environment for (GOALS.md G6.5). In this local checkout it
# is a SYMLINK to the engine repo, not a clone — agi <-> agi-tree are symlinked
# into each other because the graph literally builds the engine (see CLAUDE.md).
# Every other project gets a plain clone instead. Re-create either way:
#   ln -s /home/ubuntu/work/agi agi          # this repo
#   git clone https://github.com/CodexOperator/agi.git agi   # anywhere else
# No trailing slash: that pattern would not match a symlink.
agi

# Staged payload checkout (GOALS.md G6.3/G6.1, `grid.py checkout`). The
# committed home of these bytes is the node's own grid ref — this directory is
# a working copy of it in exactly the sense git's worktree is a working copy of
# the index, so losing it costs nothing and committing it would be the second
# copy the whole design exists to avoid.
payloads/

# Generated by the loop. nodes/ IS committed — the nodes are the thoughts.
sessions/
context/INJECTION.md
# Written by publish-engine.sh on every run, read by metrics.py
# (hours_since_successful_publish) and hooks/cc-session-start.sh (goal:g7.10).
# Machine state about this checkout, not graph content, so it is generated like
# INJECTION.md rather than committed. It is also why the marker does not live
# under nodes/: gate 0 refuses on any uncommitted change there, so a marker
# written into the graph would arm, on every run, the gate it exists to report.
context/publish-state.json
nodes.db
.chain_cache.pkl
loop.log

# Agent worktrees + local caches
.claude/worktrees/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
